          "answer": "Before replacing wildcard NOPASSWD: ALL with a Cmnd_Alias allowlist, verify whether the target user has a password set (e.g., `sudo passwd -S <user>` or check /etc/shadow). If no password is set, non-allowlisted sudo commands will fail with \"a terminal is required to read the password,\" locking the operator out. If a password exists, also confirm the operator can remember it or has a fallback, and ensure there is a tested console/break-glass recovery path. Keep the pre-deploy backup in a location the new sudoers file still permits reading so rollback is possible from the same shell.",
