          "answer": "No, refusing known-BAD values is not enough. It is described as a 'negative check' that 'closes only the failure modes you thought of, and everything the producer never emits — or that predates the field — walks straight through.' The evidence recommends instead requiring the known-good value: 'The closed form is `if meta.get(\"providers_source\") != \"session\": refuse` — require the known-good value. It rejects nothing the producer emits and everything it does not.'",
