            "same_entity": 0,
            "supersedes": 0
          },
          "answer": "Before deploying a sudoers lockdown that replaces wildcard NOPASSWD: ALL with a Cmnd_Alias allowlist, you must verify whether the target user has a password set. If no password is set, sudo for any non-allowlisted command will silently fail with 'a terminal is required to read the password', locking the operator out of all ad-hoc admin operations. Even if a password exists, ensure the operator can remember it and that console recovery is reachable and tested. Additionally, keep a pre-deploy file backup at a path the new sudoers still permits reading, and pair the tightening with a VM snapshot that has been tested for revert.",
