            "same_entity": 0,
            "supersedes": 0
          },
          "answer": "The scheduled deadman check must be cancelled or repointed in the same session when the gate is closed early. An orphaned deadman is worse than a missing one because it arrives with confident, self-contained instructions and no knowledge that the lane died, so the default behaviour is to re-run a closed experiment and post numbers that invite a reopen. The Session-Close rule (gate resolved → comment + close) is incomplete without also cancelling or repointing the paired scheduled check in the same session. When a scheduled gate task fires, the issue state must be read first: state: CLOSED means the correct output is a SUPERSEDED note on the issue, not a run. Do not treat 'the run is technically feasible' as a reason to run.",
